{"id":8351,"date":"2024-02-14T06:37:01","date_gmt":"2024-02-14T06:37:01","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/?page_id=8351"},"modified":"2024-02-14T06:41:16","modified_gmt":"2024-02-14T06:41:16","slug":"oia","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/oia\/","title":{"rendered":"Office of the International Affairs"},"content":{"rendered":"<p><strong>International Visits by Students and Faculty\u00a0<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The Fisat Business School organized an enriching International Industrial Visit (IV) to Malaysia for the S4 MBA 2021-<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">2023 Batch from March 28 to March 31, 2023. The trip provided students and accompanying staff members with invaluable exposure <\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">to international business practices and cultural experiences. Participants had the opportunity to <\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">witness firsthand the dynamics of the Malaysian business landscape and engage in insightful <\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">interactions with industry professionals. The trip included visits to several places of prominence in Malaysia, with the highlight being the tour <\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">of the Royal Selangor Pewter factory. The Royal Selangor Pewter factory visit was a remarkable <\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">experience, allowing students to witness the craftsmanship and artistry that goes into creating <\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">intricate pewter products. Students observed the various stages of pewter production, from casting <\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">to engraving, and gained insights into the company&#8217;s commitment to quality and tradition.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/1.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone wp-image-8352\" src=\"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/1.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"541\" height=\"303\" srcset=\"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/1.jpg 480w, https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/1-300x168.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 541px) 100vw, 541px\" \/><\/a><\/p>\n<p><b><br \/>\nFISAT wins Xplore 2023-education competition organized by German Multinational -Phoenix Contact<\/b><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The team from the Electronics &amp; Instrumentation Engineering Department of Federal Institute of Science &amp; Technology (FISAT), Angamaly, Kochi, won the Xplore Technology Award 2023 held in Germany in October 23,\u00a0 in the\u00a0 category \u201cSmart Technology\u201d for a sustainable world for their project &#8220;Water management at home for a sustainable world using IoT.&#8221; The project was developed by a team of students led by Aaron Sabu Joseph, Aakash Shaji, Amala Joy, Allen Simon Antony, Clinto Jose, Aravind Surendran . Lakshmi Nandakumar and Dr. Abi P Mathew were their mentors.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The team won the Xplore Technology Award 2023 by competing against 700 other teams from around the world. The award ceremony was held at the Federal Ministry for Economic Affairs and Climate Action in Berlin on October 20, 2023, which coincided with Phoenix Contact&#8217;s 100th anniversary. The winners were honored by Minister Michael Kellner, Parliamentary State Secretary.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/2.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone wp-image-8353\" src=\"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/2.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"541\" height=\"360\" srcset=\"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/2.jpg 347w, https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/2-300x200.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 541px) 100vw, 541px\" \/><\/a><\/p>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<p><strong>Dr. Jiji Antony, Dr. Kavitha P E and Mr. Pauly visited the Universiti Malaysia Pahang in Dec 2023.<br \/>\n<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/3.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone wp-image-8354\" src=\"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/3.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"540\" height=\"405\" srcset=\"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/3.jpg 469w, https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/3-300x225.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 540px) 100vw, 540px\" \/><\/a><\/p>\n<p><strong><br \/>\nMemorandum of Understanding\u00a0<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">FISAT has signed an MoU with Universiti Malaysia PAHANG AL-SULTAN ABDULLAH in Dec 2023 <\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">to promote friendship and cooperation, mutual understanding, academic, cultural and scientific thought and personnel exchange.<br \/>\n<\/span><\/p>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/4.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone wp-image-8355\" src=\"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/4.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"544\" height=\"305\" srcset=\"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/4.jpg 474w, https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/4-300x168.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 544px) 100vw, 544px\" \/><\/a><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Federal Institute of Science and Technology (FISAT) has signed a <strong>Memorandum of Understanding (MoU)<\/strong> with Universiti Teknologi Mara (UiTM) Malaysia to promote friendship and cooperation, mutual understanding, academic, cultural and scientific thought and personnel exchange in May 2023.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/5.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone wp-image-8356\" src=\"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/5.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"545\" height=\"238\" srcset=\"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/5.jpg 481w, https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/5-300x131.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 545px) 100vw, 545px\" \/><\/a><\/p>\n<p><strong><br \/>\nVisit by International Experts<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A expert talk on \u201cNavigating the future of Sustainable Built Environment\u201d was conducted by Mr. Hariram N P, Research Scholar, UMPSA Malaysia Pahang in FISAT on 29.1.2024<\/span><\/p>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/6.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone wp-image-8357\" src=\"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/6.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"545\" height=\"306\" srcset=\"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/6.jpg 602w, https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/6-300x168.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 545px) 100vw, 545px\" \/><\/a><\/p>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<p>Contact:<\/p>\n<div><strong>Office of the International Affairs\u00a0<\/strong><\/div>\n<div>Ph. no : 0484 &#8211; 2725272<\/div>\n<div>e-mail:\u00a0<a href=\"mailto:oir@fisat.ac.in\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">oir@fisat.ac.in<\/a><\/div>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>International Visits by Students and Faculty\u00a0 The Fisat Business School organized an enriching International Industrial Visit (IV) to Malaysia for the S4 MBA 2021- 2023 Batch from March 28 to March 31, 2023. The trip provided students and accompanying staff members with invaluable exposure \u00a0to international business practices and 